From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wscript: GetObject with an empty path creates the ProgID's object

Port at integration (coordinator rule: no feature lost in a drop). Drafter
7's 5524 was dropped for fast-a 3241's wscript (RECONCILE-CLOUD), whose
WScript.GetObject("", ProgID) asked for a running instance
(GetActiveObject). The WScript.GetObject and VBScript GetObject pages say
the zero-length path gives a new instance of the class (the same one only
for a single-instance class; omitting the path is an error), as 5524 did.
The empty path now creates the object. 5524's gate (wscript) passes.

Mutant: SG_MUTANT_WSH_GETOBJ_ACTIVE (wscript gate).
---
diff --git a/programs/wscript/host.c b/programs/wscript/host.c
--- a/programs/wscript/host.c
+++ b/programs/wscript/host.c
@@ -829,12 +829,21 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI Host_GetObject(IHost *iface, BSTR Pathname, BSTR ProgID,
 #endif
 
     if(!Pathname) {
-        /* a running instance of the class */
+        /* the path is required: an empty one (and, from C, none) asks for an instance of the
+         * class, a new one unless the class is registered single-instance (WScript.GetObject and
+         * VBScript GetObject docs: "" returns a new object instance; ported at integration from
+         * drafter 7's 5524, which the kept GetActiveObject lacked) */
         GUID guid;
 
         hres = CLSIDFromProgID(ProgID, &guid);
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_WSH_GETOBJ_ACTIVE
         if(SUCCEEDED(hres))
             hres = GetActiveObject(&guid, NULL, &unk);
+#else
+        if(SUCCEEDED(hres))
+            hres = CoCreateInstance(&guid, NULL, CLSCTX_INPROC_SERVER|CLSCTX_LOCAL_SERVER,
+                    &IID_IUnknown, (void**)&unk);
+#endif
     }else if(ProgID) {
         /* a new object of the class that loads the file */
         IPersistFile *persist;
